## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-region coherence, stampede prevention, and combined Redis/Memcached strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed cache invalidation across regions
- Versioned keys and pub/sub invalidations
- Read-through vs write-through choices
- Dead-letter handling for partition faults

## Code Example
```javascript
// Update path
const ver = await redis.incr(`res:${id}:ver`);
await redis.publish(`cache:invalidate:${id}`, ver);

// Read path
let [value, verCached] = memcache.get(`res:${id}:val`);
const currentVer = await redis.get(`res:${id}:ver`);
if (verCached !== currentVer) {
  value = fetchFromSourceAndUpdateCaches(id, currentVer);
  memcache.set(`res:${id}:val`, value);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle late subscribers to invalidation?
- How would you adapt for ultra-hot keys with skyrocketing write rates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of token binding and multi-idp flows in production.

## Key Concepts
- Token binding with cnf
- per-tenant key rotation
- KMS/JWK management
- auditing and revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Issuer (simplified)
const tenantKwk = getTenantKey(tenantId); // {kid, jwk}
const token = jwt.sign({sub, iss: 'gateway', aud: tenantAud}, tenantPrivateKey, { algorithm:'ES256', header: { kid: tenantKwk.kid }, nonce: crypto.randomBytes(16).toString('hex'), cnf: { jwk: tenantKwk.jwk } });

// Verifier
const decoded = jwt.verify(token, tenantPublicKey, { algorithms:['ES256'] });
if (!compareJwk(decoded.cnf.jwk, getTenantBoundJwk(tenantId))) throw new Error('binding mismatch');
```

